{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4BH9YkLUttaSn6oHTy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The migration is done: `config.ini` is replaced by `config.toml`, the loader reads it with `tomllib`, and both tests pass (2 of 2, on Python 3.14).\n\n- **`config.toml`** (new): the same sections and keys as before. Strings are quoted, `port` and `pool_size` and `max_upload_mb` are ints, `timeout` is the float `2.5`, and `debug` and `beta` are real booleans.\n- **`app/config.py`**: `load_config` now opens the file in binary mode and returns `tomllib.load(f)`. The default path changed from `config.ini` to `config.toml`. The return value is the same nested dict of sections, now with typed values.\n- **`tests/test_config.py`**: I added `test_value_types`, which checks the int, float and bool types and their values, since the existing test only checked the section names and the host string.\n- **`config.ini`**: deleted.\n\nNothing is committed. The working tree has the four changes above.\n\nOne behaviour change to be aware of: the old `configparser` version returned `{}` when the file was missing. Now `load_config` raises `FileNotFoundError`. I think that's the better behaviour for a config file, but say if you want the old silent fallback back."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":50144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3701},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a9788c-e292-446e-b323-13b31e5eadec","uuid":"91df198a-6538-4e80-8645-874b7967b001","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:26:49.736Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4BGrg6h5muXmAVXmu4"}
